# This repository is developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. That is harmless for anything git carries
# end to end, but the F-Droid recipe is different: it is uploaded from the
# working tree straight into fdroiddata, and fdroidserver's rewritemeta
# check compares it byte-for-byte against LF-normalised output. A CRLF copy
# fails that check on every single line, with no hint that line endings are
# the cause. Pin it to LF so the file on disk is always the file to upload.
fdroid/*.yml text eol=lf

# Uploaded to the same place and read the same way.
fastlane/metadata/**/*.txt text eol=lf
